[32m+[m[32m## Milestone 6: First Real SQL Tool[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mObjective: add one safe production tool over `clean_jobs` so the agent can answer real job-data questions while keeping the public API response simple.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWhat to implement:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- one SQL tool exposed through the agent runtime[m
[32m+[m[32m- schema/context builder for `clean_jobs`[m
[32m+[m[32m- SQL generation prompt for the tool path[m
[32m+[m[32m- strict read-only SQL validation[m
[32m+[m[32m- validated execution against the database[m
[32m+[m[32m- table shaping for internal tool/debug use[m
[32m+[m[32m- refusal path for unsafe or unsupported SQL[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBehavior rule:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- if the user asks about jobs, counts, salaries, locations, titles, companies, filters, or trends that depend on `clean_jobs`, the agent must use the SQL tool[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSuccess criteria:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- the agent can answer one real `clean_jobs` question end-to-end[m
[32m+[m[32m- unsafe SQL is rejected before execution[m
[32m+[m[32m- the public response includes a natural-language answer[m
[32m+[m[32m- tool output remains structured internally for tracing and future UX expansion[m
[32m+[m[32m- the SQL path is traceable in Langfuse[m
[32m+[m[32m- at least one success-path and one refusal/failure-path test exist[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mImportant note:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis milestone should come before memory. A useful InternHunter MVP is defined first by trustworthy job-data answers, then by conversational refinement.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mResponse note:[m
[32m+[m
